{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And this people will rise.</b> It is impossible for [the verse] to be joined with what precedes it, for what is the meaning of 'this people' and 'will whore'?" "And the meaning of <b>and will whore.</b> To depart in his thought from His domain." "<b>After the gods of the foreigner of the land.</b> We know that HaShem is one, and change comes from the receivers, and HaShem does not change His deeds, for all are in wisdom. And from the service of HaShem to guard the power of reception according to the place — therefore it is written 'the statute of the gods of the land' — therefore Jacob said 'Remove the gods of the foreigner.' And the opposite of the place cleaves to forbidden relations, which are 'flesh of near kin.' And the discerning will understand." "And the meaning of <b>in its midst.</b> A stranger of the land, as if it said 'and will whore after the gods of a foreign people,' who are the gods of the land. And the nearer reading is that 'in its midst' refers to the land, for the masculine form is found [used for land], as in 'and the land did not bear them.' 'The land was deceived.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:41.928096052Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}